instuection set for cpu11

(000000) SCA - Prompts the user to enter an 8 bit number, sets it to the accumilator
(000001) HAL - Halts the program
(000010) LOD {d1} - Sets the accumilator to whatever $d1 is
(000011) CLR - clears and dumps the memory
(000100) TAC {d1} - sets memory address d1 to the current counter
(000101) LDA {d1} - Copy data from memory address $d1 into Accumulator
(000110) STA {d1} - Load Accumilator into memory address $d1
(000111) ADD {d1} - adds memory contents $d1 and accum together, for example d1= 00001001 accum= 10001010, answer= 10010011
(001000) SUB {d1} - like add, but subtracts instead.
(001001) AND {d1} - Bitwise AND memory contents with Accumulator; then stores to accumilator.
(001010) ORR {d1} - Bitwise OR memory contents with Accumulator; then stores to accumilator.
(001011) JMP {d1} - Unconditionally change execution flow to $d1
(001100) JZE {d1} - Conditionally jump to $d1 if the Zero Flag is set.
(001101) JMF {d1} - Like JMP, but it jumps to the value stored at address $d1
(001110) JZF {d1} - Like JZE, but it jumps to the value stored at address $d1
(001111) DIS - takes the first 8 memory addresses (00000000-00000111) and outputs then as a display-like image,
 data inside the address is the x value, and the actual address is the y value
(010000) BLK - HE'S BACKKKKK
